  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Where the distance comes from",
      "items": [
        "Phase-based ranging reads the phase rotation across scheduled carrier frequencies, resolving to ±1 to 3 cm in line of sight",
        "When multipath obscures the carrier phase the radio supplements it with round-trip timing, which is why rangingMode reports pbr, rtt or hybrid",
        "A multipath impulse-response filter runs before a target is reported, so confidence is a measured value rather than a constant"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Why this resists a relay attack",
      "items": [
        "Every subevent carries cryptographic nonce sequencing, so a recorded exchange cannot be replayed",
        "A relayed signal cannot preserve phase-path integrity, which is what distinguishes this from classic BLE keyless entry",
        "securityLevel reports whether the exchange ran in high_security mode rather than assuming it did"
      ]
    }
  ]
